WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.780
Today there is a growing awareness that mental well-being needs to be given as much attention as physical health.
如今，人们越来越意识到，心理健康需要得到和身体健康同样多的关注。

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:19.240
Faced with heavy academic pressure, fierce competition and a fast pace of life, more and more people suffer from anxiety, stress or low mood.
面对繁重的学业压力、激烈的竞争和快节奏的生活，越来越多的人饱受焦虑、压力或情绪低落之苦。

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.840
Mental well-being deserves such attention because it affects every part of our lives.
心理健康之所以值得如此关注，是因为它影响着我们生活的方方面面。

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:35.010
Many students, for example, are physically fit but so anxious before exams that they can hardly focus in class or enjoy time with friends.
比如，许多学生身体很健康，却在考试前焦虑得几乎无法专心上课，也无法享受和朋友在一起的时光。

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:43.270
In fact, the mind and the body are closely linked: long-term stress may cause sleep problems and weaken the immune system.
事实上，身体和心理是紧密相连的：长期的压力可能导致睡眠问题，并削弱免疫系统。

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:53.330
Yet unlike a fever or a broken arm, mental health problems are often invisible and easy to ignore, and some people even feel ashamed to seek help.
然而，与发烧或胳膊骨折不同，心理健康问题往往是看不见的，容易被忽视，有些人甚至羞于寻求帮助。

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:58.270
Therefore, we should care for our minds as carefully as we care for our bodies.
因此，我们应当像关爱自己的身体一样，细心呵护自己的心灵。

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:04.910
Individuals can keep a regular routine, exercise often and talk with friends when they feel down.
个人可以保持规律的作息、经常锻炼，并在情绪低落时找朋友聊聊。

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:09.200
If the problem persists, they should seek professional help.
如果问题持续存在，他们就应当寻求专业帮助。

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.740
Colleges should provide easily accessible counseling services and help remove the stigma surrounding mental health.
高校应当提供便于获得的心理咨询服务，并帮助消除围绕心理健康问题的偏见。

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:22.820
After all, a truly healthy life requires both a sound body and a sound mind.
毕竟，真正健康的生活既需要健全的身体，也需要健全的心灵。
